How can I use Scala to classify a word as a noun, verb, adjective, or adverb? Specifically, how can I classify the word "quick"?
[Scala code]
Here is an example code that uses the Stanford CoreNLP library to classify words:
import edu.stanford.nlp.simple._
object WordClassification {
  def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {
    val inputText = "quick"
    val doc = new Document(inputText)
    val word = doc.sentences().head.word(0)
    val pos = doc.sentences().head.posTag(0)
    pos match {
      case "NN" => println(s"$word is a noun.")
      case "VB" => println(s"$word is a verb.")
      case "JJ" => println(s"$word is an adjective.")
      case "RB" => println(s"$word is an adverb.")
      case _ => println(s"Unable to classify $word.")
    }
  }
}
This code uses the Stanford CoreNLP library to analyze the part-of-speech of the input word, and then classifies it as a noun, verb, adjective, or adverb. Note that you will need to add the Stanford CoreNLP library to your project dependencies in order to use this code.

