Secondly, the act of theft also violates the principle of procedural justice, which refers to the fairness and impartiality of the procedures used to determine outcomes. In this case, the protagonist did not follow the proper procedures for obtaining the item they wanted. Instead, they resorted to stealing it, which is an unfair and unjust way of obtaining goods. This violates the principle of procedural justice, which requires that individuals should be treated fairly and impartially in all procedures and decisions.
The presence of CCTV footage and resulting police investigation is relevant in evaluating the situation from an ethical perspective. The use of CCTV footage and police investigation can be seen as a way of ensuring justice and upholding the principles of fairness and impartiality. The CCTV footage provides evidence of the theft, which can be used to determine the guilt of the protagonist. The police investigation ensures that the procedures used to determine the guilt of the protagonist are fair and impartial.
