To generate a set of lexically equivalent words for each word in an English sentence using PHP code, you can use a computational linguistic model such as WordNet. WordNet is a lexical database that groups English words into sets of synonyms called synsets, and provides short definitions and usage examples for each synset.
To use WordNet in PHP, you can use the PHP WordNet package, which provides a simple interface to the WordNet database. Here's an example code snippet that demonstrates how to use PHP WordNet to generate a set of lexically equivalent words for each word in an English sentence:
```
<?php
require_once 'vendor/autoload.php';
use \MIT\WordNet\WordNet;
// Initialize WordNet
$wordnet = new WordNet();
// Define the input sentence
$sentence = "The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.";
// Tokenize the sentence into words
$words = explode(" ", $sentence);
// Generate a set of lexically equivalent words for each word
foreach ($words as $word) {
    $synsets = $wordnet->synsets($word);
    $equivalent_words = array();
    foreach ($synsets as $synset) {
        $words = $synset->words();
        $equivalent_words = array_merge($equivalent_words, $words);
    }
    echo $word . ": " . implode(", ", $equivalent_words) . "\n";
}
?>
```
